HST Office: Word VBA in HST Writer (owner goal for 1.0.0-beta.5: at least 20 of the 24 Word cases of
tests/runtime/vba_cases.py; now 20/24), Word document events, and Vietnamese text in VBA projects.

Object model (oovbaapi word/*.idl, sw/source/ui/vba):
- Paragraph.Alignment and Paragraph.Format; ParagraphFormat.Alignment read and wrote the short
  ParaAdjust property as the enum, so it always reported "left" and setting it did nothing.
- Table.Cell(Row, Column) and Cell.Range.
- Document.Words and Document.Sentences (new vbatextunits.*: collections of Ranges built with the
  word/sentence cursors; Count, Item, For Each).
- ListFormat.ApplyBulletDefault (default bullet list style "List 1", toggles like Word).
- Find.Execute without replacement searched after the range instead of inside it, reused the
  replacement of an earlier Execute, and did not redefine the Range to the found text.
- Bookmarks.Add made a collapsed bookmark (insertTextContent without absorb).
- Sections(n).Headers/Footers(...).Range switches an unused header/footer on instead of failing.
- Document.Range(0, 0) / Range(n, n) are collapsed at that position (they were at the end of the
  text), and a collapsed Range has no text (it returned the next character).

Events and VBA mode (sw core):
- Word VBA events and code names ran only for Word 97 files (mime "application/msword"). They now
  also run for .docx/.docm and for documents whose Basic is in VBA mode, the event processor
  starts with the VBA globals (as in Calc), and an exception in a handler or a missing ThisDocument
  module no longer ends the office (SwDocShell::Notify).
- .odt keeps the VBA mode and project name of its macros (document settings VBACompatibilityMode,
  VBAProjectName), so Document_Open and the VBA object model work after saving in ODF too.

Code page (oox VbaExport):
- A VBA project whose code page cannot hold its code (Vietnamese text in a project made with a
  Western code page) is saved in Windows-1258 instead of turning letters into '?'. An unset code
  page no longer replaces the thread encoding with DONTKNOW.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); the new
sw/source/ui/vba/vbatextunits.* files are MPL-2.0 like their neighbours.
Test: tests/runtime/check-vba.py, tests/runtime/check-vba-editor.py.
